message:
{{#is_alert}}Fleet LLM spend in the trailing 24h is over $12 — runaway territory. The busiest shipping day so far (2026-09-02, a dozen PR reviews) was $5.56; ten uncached reviews or a loop get here in an hour or two.{{/is_alert}}
{{#is_warning}}Fleet LLM spend in the trailing 24h is over $6 — above any day seen so far; a glance, not a page.{{/is_warning}}

Triage on the [fleet dashboard](https://app.datadoghq.com/dashboard/bwm-uny-qqs):
- **Avg cost per model call** flat -> volume spike (who shipped a lot? a PR train is benign — 2026-09-02 was $5.56 at a normal $0.017/call).
- **Avg cost per call** stepped up -> price change: model swap, prompt growth, or a broken cache prefix (check the caching row). The companion monitor "Fleet LLM cost per call — price signal" watches this directly.
- **Cost by ml_app** names the spender; **cost by model** says what it ran on.

Metric is nanodollars; the query divides by 1e9 so thresholds read in dollars. Guardrail from RC1-349; thresholds raised by RC1-377 (2026-09-03) from $1.50/$3 after four of five days crossed the old warn line — the daily total tracks PR volume, so this line is set where only a failure can reach it.

